Navigation note (covenant #7 — no predecessor bypass): the web route /timeline is a standalone route
(web App.tsx `<Route path="timeline">`), distinct from /analytics and /statistics. No free alias maps to it
(.analytics is owned by the DONE sibling StatisticsPage), so a dedicated .timeline AppRoute case is added — the
honest representation of a separate page. pathSegment defaults to "timeline", so AppRouteParser resolves /timeline
directly (firstSegment == pathSegment) — deep-linkable with no parser edit. The existing RouteTests invariants hold:
testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment (segment "timeline" is unique) and testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup (.timeline added
to the .insights group switch). AppRoute's two exhaustive switches (systemImage, group) were both updated; no other
exhaustive switch over AppRoute exists (WatchDeepLink is its own enum). The model is built @MainActor in the
registration enum and captured, mirroring the sibling *RouteRegistration enums.

